Local adaptations:
  - Contract and task-user roles are black-box; the adversary can inspect source.
  - Contract checks derive expectations first; task-user receives a goal, not steps.
  - Browser-only driving is generalized to CLI, HTTP API, and package interfaces.
  - Reports use PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED, target, expected/observed results, and evidence.
  - Reference examples, reflection hooks, and absent helper-file dependencies are omitted.
  - Cleanup and report-without-fixing instructions are retained across all three roles.
  - OpenCode metadata grants unrestricted shell access and inherits the parent model.

